WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:12.244
Molly and her mother were shopping for clothes on a Saturday afternoon, but every time Molly found something

2
00:00:12.284 --> 00:00:16.567
she liked, her mother said, "That's too expensive, Molly."

3
00:00:17.508 --> 00:00:20.590
In the end, Molly's mother chose an ugly pair of pants.

4
00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:23.272
"I'm never going to wear them!"

5
00:00:23.812 --> 00:00:24.713
Molly complained.

6
00:00:25.454 --> 00:00:28.135
Molly's mother was very careful about spending money.

7
00:00:30.832 --> 00:00:33.875
"Money doesn't grow on trees," she always said.

8
00:00:33.895 --> 00:00:36.477
"Oh, hi, Molly!"

9
00:00:37.297 --> 00:00:41.241
It was Molly's friend Erica, who was shopping with her mother in the same store.

10
00:00:41.261 --> 00:00:43.022
"Hi, Erica!"

11
00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:44.543
Molly said.

12
00:00:44.563 --> 00:00:48.387
"Things are so expensive these days, aren't they?"

13
00:00:49.107 --> 00:00:50.168
said Erica's mom.

14
00:00:51.169 --> 00:00:53.771
"Yes, I can't believe the prices!"

15
00:00:54.752 --> 00:00:55.813
agreed Molly's mother.

16
00:00:55.833 --> 00:00:58.635
"Mom, I want that!"

17
00:00:59.075 --> 00:01:02.065
said Erica, pointing to an expensive face cleanser.

18
00:01:05.385 --> 00:01:06.406
"Of course, honey.

19
00:01:06.926 --> 00:01:07.806
One? Two?

20
00:01:08.366 --> 00:01:09.727
No, let's take three."

21
00:01:10.787 --> 00:01:13.488
Erica's mother put some bottles into her shopping cart.

22
00:01:13.508 --> 00:01:15.928
"Well, we should get going.

23
00:01:16.268 --> 00:01:18.309
Good-bye!" "Mom?

24
00:01:18.749 --> 00:01:20.069
Can I have some too?"

25
00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:21.470
asked Molly.

26
00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:29.572
"Honey, this is really overpriced," Molly's mother answered, "but if you want, we can get one."

27
00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:33.339
"No, I want more," Molly said.

28
00:01:37.662 --> 00:01:40.725
is more than enough," her mother said firmly.

29
00:01:41.546 --> 00:01:45.569
Molly's family wasn't poor, but her parents didn't buy Molly whatever she wanted.

30
00:01:45.589 --> 00:01:49.412
"Money isn't everything," her father would say.

31
00:01:49.432 --> 00:01:53.136
"The real valuable things in life cannot be bought with money."

32
00:01:53.156 --> 00:01:57.700
"And money doesn't grow on trees," her mother would add.

33
00:02:00.544 --> 00:02:04.387
The next day, Molly and her friends were looking at magazines at Jenny's house.

34
00:02:04.407 --> 00:02:08.290
"Wow! I'm going to ask my mom to buy me this!"

35
00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:11.972
Esther exclaimed, pointing to the dress in a fashion ad.

36
00:02:11.992 --> 00:02:14.554
"Oh, this is so nice!

37
00:02:14.954 --> 00:02:17.756
I'll tell my dad I want this for my birthday!"

38
00:02:18.317 --> 00:02:19.037
Sharon said.

39
00:02:19.057 --> 00:02:21.119
"See what I got?"

40
00:02:21.659 --> 00:02:23.360
Jenny held up a pretty blue shirt.

41
00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:25.662
"It's so cute!

42
00:02:26.002 --> 00:02:26.983
How much was it?"

43
00:02:27.603 --> 00:02:28.244
asked Sharon.

44
00:02:31.356 --> 00:02:33.637
"I don't know, but it has a matching hat.

45
00:02:33.997 --> 00:02:37.219
See?" Molly felt so jealous of her friends.

46
00:02:37.239 --> 00:02:40.920
"Why are my parents so stingy with money?"

47
00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:42.601
she thought to herself.

48
00:02:43.821 --> 00:02:46.742
As she was walking home, something on the sidewalk caught her eye.

49
00:02:47.403 --> 00:02:48.743
Molly bent down to pick it up.

50
00:02:49.243 --> 00:02:49.944
It was a purse.

51
00:02:50.944 --> 00:02:52.625
"Someone must have dropped it!"

52
00:02:53.185 --> 00:02:54.586
she said, looking for the owner.

53
00:02:57.267 --> 00:02:59.988
There was no one around, so Molly opened the purse.

54
00:03:00.936 --> 00:03:01.596
She gasped!

55
00:03:01.936 --> 00:03:03.777
The purse was filled with cash!

56
00:03:03.797 --> 00:03:05.338
"Oh no!

57
00:03:05.918 --> 00:03:06.999
What should I do?"

58
00:03:07.659 --> 00:03:08.339
Molly wondered.

59
00:03:08.359 --> 00:03:14.441
"I should take it to the police station, but what if the owner never comes to claim it?

60
00:03:15.202 --> 00:03:20.604
Maybe I could take just a little bit of money and then take it to the police station?"

61
00:03:23.925 --> 00:03:28.167
At home, Molly did not tell her parents about the purse and went upstairs to bed.

62
00:03:29.047 --> 00:03:34.347
As she thought about keeping the money, a strange feeling stirred inside of her, something she had never

63
00:03:34.427 --> 00:03:35.088
felt before.

64
00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:38.291
Two voices began to argue in her head.

65
00:03:38.311 --> 00:03:41.753
"Take the money," said Molly the Red.

66
00:03:41.774 --> 00:03:44.876
"No! Turn it in to the police!"

67
00:03:45.477 --> 00:03:46.438
said Molly the White.

68
00:03:50.881 --> 00:03:52.203
one will know if you take it!"

69
00:03:52.823 --> 00:03:53.444
said the Red.

70
00:03:53.464 --> 00:03:55.585
"It's not yours.

71
00:03:55.886 --> 00:03:57.067
You can't keep it!"

72
00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:58.288
said the White.

73
00:03:59.124 --> 00:04:03.286
Molly wasn't sure which voice to listen to, but when she thought of all the things she could

74
00:04:03.326 --> 00:04:05.467
buy, she decided to take the money.

75
00:04:05.487 --> 00:04:08.809
"Now you can buy anything you want!"

76
00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:10.470
said Molly the Red.

77
00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:12.211
"No, Molly!

78
00:04:12.311 --> 00:04:13.172
Don't do it!"

79
00:04:13.832 --> 00:04:14.832
Molly the White begged.

80
00:04:17.214 --> 00:04:19.575
Molly felt that strange feeling grow stronger.

81
00:04:19.595 --> 00:04:22.637
"Now you can be like your friends!"

82
00:04:23.517 --> 00:04:24.918
the Red whispered excitedly.

83
00:04:25.878 --> 00:04:28.840
Molly smiled and ignored the strange feeling inside.

84
00:04:29.864 --> 00:04:32.885
At the store, she realized it felt powerful to have so much money.

85
00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:39.188
"I'll take these two, please," she said, handing two pairs of shoes to the sales clerk.

86
00:04:40.328 --> 00:04:42.129
"Here you go," smiled the clerk.

87
00:04:42.149 --> 00:04:43.910
"Thank you and come again!"

88
00:04:46.811 --> 00:04:51.113
Molly also bought a new shirt and jeans, and decided to wear them on her way home.

89
00:04:52.113 --> 00:04:54.634
As she left the store, she bumped into her friends.

90
00:04:54.654 --> 00:04:57.735
"Molly! You look so stylish!"

91
00:04:58.456 --> 00:04:59.396
admired Erica.

92
00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:01.681
"Are those new jeans?"

93
00:05:02.361 --> 00:05:03.041
asked Jenny.

94
00:05:03.061 --> 00:05:05.742
"I love that shirt!"

95
00:05:06.403 --> 00:05:07.303
exclaimed Sharon.

96
00:05:07.323 --> 00:05:10.664
"Where did you get the money to buy these things?"

97
00:05:11.285 --> 00:05:11.945
Jenny asked.

98
00:05:17.227 --> 00:05:20.969
my mom gave money Molly stammered.

99
00:05:20.989 --> 00:05:23.130
"It's none of your business!"

100
00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:24.510
she burst out.

101
00:05:25.531 --> 00:05:30.209
After she spent the rest of the day buying whatever she wanted, Molly took her purchases up to

102
00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:30.729
her bedroom.

103
00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:33.531
That strange feeling nudged at her heart again.

104
00:05:33.551 --> 00:05:36.112
"What is this I'm feeling?"

105
00:05:36.632 --> 00:05:37.173
she wondered.

106
00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:39.214
It was really bothering her.

107
00:05:39.234 --> 00:05:43.877
"I bought everything I wanted, so why am I not happy?"

108
00:05:46.238 --> 00:05:48.799
Molly picked up the empty purse and opened it up again.

109
00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:50.820
Inside was a letter.

110
00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:56.824
"Dear Mommy," the letter began, "I wish Daddy would recover soon.

111
00:05:57.704 --> 00:06:01.286
I don't have a lot, but here is some money I saved from working.

112
00:06:02.126 --> 00:06:04.407
Please use it for Daddy's hospital bills.

113
00:06:05.328 --> 00:06:07.288
I just want Daddy to be well again."

114
00:06:08.849 --> 00:06:11.610
As Molly read the letter, her eyes welled up with tears.

115
00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:13.611
"What have I done?

116
00:06:14.332 --> 00:06:15.412
What have I done?"

117
00:06:16.172 --> 00:06:17.093
she cried aloud.

118
00:06:17.913 --> 00:06:18.794
Her heart was aching.

119
00:06:18.814 --> 00:06:21.315
"What kind of person am I?

120
00:06:21.715 --> 00:06:22.635
I'm a thief!"

121
00:06:23.276 --> 00:06:23.776
she moaned.

122
00:06:24.712 --> 00:06:25.813
"I hate myself!

123
00:06:26.233 --> 00:06:27.494
I hate myself!"

124
00:06:27.514 --> 00:06:29.736
"Molly! Molly!

125
00:06:30.117 --> 00:06:31.117
Wake up, honey!"

126
00:06:31.938 --> 00:06:33.379
Molly's mother gently shook her.

127
00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:37.563
Molly was in her room, but the shopping bags and new shoes were gone.

128
00:06:37.583 --> 00:06:43.527
"You were having a nightmare," her mother said.

129
00:06:44.348 --> 00:06:46.069
Molly felt something against her back.

130
00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:49.192
It was the purse, and the money was still inside.

131
00:06:50.093 --> 00:06:51.093
Molly was relieved.

132
00:06:51.514 --> 00:06:55.536
She explained how she had found the purse, and confessed that she had wanted to keep the money.

133
00:06:55.556 --> 00:06:59.858
"I'm glad it was just a bad dream," Molly said.

134
00:06:59.878 --> 00:07:04.939
"Me too, honey, and I'm proud of you," her mother said.

135
00:07:04.959 --> 00:07:08.820
"How can you be proud of me?

136
00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:10.720
I wanted to keep the money!"

137
00:07:11.321 --> 00:07:12.001
Molly said.

138
00:07:12.021 --> 00:07:13.841
"But you didn't.

139
00:07:14.702 --> 00:07:16.922
You know that strange feeling you had?"

140
00:07:17.422 --> 00:07:18.162
her mother asked.

141
00:07:18.182 --> 00:07:20.503
"That was your conscience.

142
00:07:21.363 --> 00:07:23.584
It was telling you to do what was right.

143
00:07:24.508 --> 00:07:30.431
In the end, you listened to your conscience, your heart, and that's what's most important."

144
00:07:30.451 --> 00:07:39.455
"Mom, I learned that having the things I want doesn't make me happy," Molly said.

145
00:07:39.475 --> 00:07:42.417
"Money can't buy me happiness."

146
00:07:43.417 --> 00:07:44.518
"You're a good girl.

147
00:07:45.178 --> 00:07:48.960
It's good deeds that make a good heart," her mother said lovingly.
